{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for the constants \\(c_2\\), \\(c_1\\), and \\(c_0\\) in the equation\n\\[x^3 + x^2 - 5 = (x - 3)^3 + c_2 (x - 3)^2 + c_1 (x - 3) + c_0,\\]\nwe will expand the right-hand side and then compare coefficients with the left-hand side.\n\nFirst, expand \\((x-3)^3\\):\n\\[\n(x-3)^3 = x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27.\n\\]\nNow, let's expand the full expression on the right-hand side:\n\\[\n(x-3)^3 + c_2 (x-3)^2 + c_1 (x-3) + c_0 = x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27 + c_2 (x^2 - 6x + 9) + c_1 (x - 3) + c_0.\n\\]\nSimplify the expression by distributing and combining like terms:\n\\[\nx^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27 + c_2 x^2 - 6c_2 x + 9c_2 + c_1 x - 3c_1 + c_0 = x^3 + (c_2 - 9)x^2 + (27 - 6c_2 + c_1)x + (-27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0).\n\\]\nWe now compare the coefficients of the expanded form with the original polynomial \\(x^3 + x^2 - 5\\):\n\\[\nx^3 + (c_2 - 9)x^2 + (27 - 6c_2 + c_1)x + (-27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0) = x^3 + x^2 - 5.\n\\]\nBy comparing the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n1. \\(c_2 - 9 = 1\\),\n2. \\(27 - 6c_2 + c_1 = 1\\),\n3. \\(-27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0 = -5\\).\n\n","prefix_end":1034,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,279,18021,17767,66,62,17,59,701,17767,66,62,16,59,701,323,17767,66,62,15,57758,304,279,23606,198,78045,87,61,18,488,856,61,17,481,220,20,284,320,87,481,220,18,29776,18,488,272,62,17,320,87,481,220,18,29776,17,488,272,62,16,320,87,481,220,18,8,488,272,62,15,26266,921,896,686,9225,279,1290,24413,3108,323,1221,9429,36829,448,279,2115,24413,3108,382,5338,11,9225,1124,1188,87,12,18,29776,18,59,982,59,9640,2075,12,18,29776,18,284,856,61,18,481,220,24,87,61,17,488,220,17,22,87,481,220,17,22,624,59,921,7039,11,1077,594,9225,279,2480,7493,389,279,1290,24413,3108,510,59,9640,2075,12,18,29776,18,488,272,62,17,320,87,12,18,29776,17,488,272,62,16,320,87,12,18,8,488,272,62,15,284,856,61,18,481,